  "detail": null,
  "summary": "I worked through all 13 results inbox items: the 8 that were there this morning and 5 that arrived while I worked. 12 are closed. One is still open on purpose: a preliminary chest X-ray for Leslie Parisian (pt-0007, inbox-a0002) that has no final report yet, so policy says to leave it open. Two things need you: cancelling an imaging order my tools couldn't cancel (task-t0034, Raj Patel), and telling staff not to draw an extra blood test for Walter Brennan.\n\n**Things that need follow-up**\n- **Walter Brennan (pt-0008) – potassium 6.4, now real.** At first the lab flagged the sample as hemolyzed (broken-down blood cells can make potassium read falsely high). Under that rule I ordered an urgent repeat blood panel by Monday (sr-t0015) and messaged him.\n  - At 07:55 the lab corrected the result: the hemolysis comment belonged to another patient, so 6.4 stands. I switched to the critical-potassium rule.\n  - I sent a stat message to the on-call pool (comm-t0020), ordered a stat blood panel for today (sr-t0019), and sent him a correction asking him to come in today.\n  - None of his medications raise potassium. I left metoprolol in place because of his heart disease.\n  - The Monday order (sr-t0015) is replaced by today's stat order but couldn't be cancelled, so it shouldn't be drawn separately.\n- **Raj Patel (pt-0006) – lung screening plan changed.** His CT for blood in the urine found no kidney or bladder cause. It showed the 4 mm lung nodule his screening program already follows, so I ordered the next screening low-dose chest CT for spring 2027.\n  - Later the screening centre sent an addendum to his April 2026 scan: a new 5 mm nodule in the right lung, Lung-RADS 3 (probably benign), repeat in 6 months.\n  - I ordered a new low-dose chest CT by 2026-11-14 (sr-t0032), added a tracking task, and sent him a correction.\n  - The 2027 order (sr-t0001) and its tracking task (task-t0002) are now wrong. My tools can't cancel either, so task-t0034 asks you to cancel both.\n- **Acute kidney injury (sudden creatinine rise), 3 patients.** Each got an urgent repeat blood panel by Monday 10/26, an urgent patient message and a note:\n  - **Leslie Parisian (pt-0007):** creatinine 1.64, up from 0.98 about 35 hours earlier (sr-t0008).\n  - **Carol Whitfield (pt-0033):** the clinic result of 1.31 alone didn't meet the rule, because the 0.84 from 10/21 was withdrawn as entered in error. A later urgent-care result of 1.78, about 9 hours after the 1.31, does meet it (sr-t0025).\n  - **Helen Marchetti (pt-0064):** the September ED result of 1.36 didn't meet the rule. Two newly filed results did: 1.48 on 10/22, up from 0.88 on 10/21 (sr-t0024).\n\n**Closed with no action needed**\n- **Edra Ondricka (pt-0016):** TSH normal. The potassium of 6.3 was corrected by the lab to 4.4 (a machine calibration fault).\n- **Leslie Parisian (pt-0007), chest CT angiogram:** the inbox had the preliminary read, which described a lung nodule. The final report says there was no blood clot and no nodule (it was a blood vessel), and no lung follow-up is needed.\n\nEach result that needed action has a note citing it and was closed with links to its orders, messages and tasks. I didn't touch your messages queue: its 6 refill requests came in before today and fall outside the results inbox.",
